From 65738d62d85818b94322bb97386e493bd2c23ec8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fardjad Davari <public@fardjad.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:08:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix: preserve runtime context for swarm pop-outs

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: Resume local swarm children in their parent runtime
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: upstream-candidate
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: none
X-Jcode-Patch-File: 0006-candidate-preserve-runtime-for-swarm-popouts.patch

Patch intent:
Carry effective local session-storage and runtime paths plus the selected
server socket through swarm pop-out requests to the terminal child. Preserve
that allowlisted runtime identity across terminal, companion, and hook launch
boundaries, retaining the new pane's identity and shared terminal behavior.

Why it exists:
Multiplexer servers can create shells without the requesting client's runtime
environment. A selected child then appears missing despite existing in the
parent runtime. Contextual companion requests use a distinct operation so an
older daemon rejects the request instead of silently dropping the new context;
the client then safely falls back to its local launch path. Filter runtime keys
at construction and wire serialization/deserialization so secrets and arbitrary
metadata never cross the boundary. The shared Windows launcher honors
JCODE_TERMINAL and keeps cmd as its fallback; it never consults the separate
app-core-only JCODE_RESUME_TERMINAL override, which the separate app-core API
retains for its existing callers. Deterministic configured-selection and
cmd-fallback tests in the terminal-launch suite pin that behavior. A Unix
fake-socket regression sends both contextual and legacy requests through the
production socket handler and its injected terminal-launch seam, verifying
filtered runtime and preserved command metadata without launching hardware. Its
temporary socket fixture uses a short system temp root to remain within Unix
socket path limits. Hooks receive a safely quoted runtime-aware invocation at
the actual argv execution boundary. Keep no-context callers and hook argv
unchanged. SSH pop-outs remain unchanged, not a new SSH resume implementation.
Ordinary local-daemon TUI clients use runtime context even though App::is_remote
is true; only the actual SSH transport predicate keeps the previous launch
behavior. Executable selection and issue #1119 are not addressed.

Upstream integration points:
TUI swarm pop-out builds a TerminalCommand and routes local launches through the
shared jcode-terminal-launch entry point while retaining the SSH client
launcher. app-core captures storage::jcode_dir and storage::runtime_dir,
preserves optional API socket and update control, and adds explicit socket
resume args. TerminalCommand carries allowlisted runtime values separately from
spawn and client-terminal metadata. Unix terminal argv and hook shell-command
metadata carry safely quoted values; hooks and non-Unix process launches
receive runtime process environment. Companion client/server use the
SpawnTerminalWithRuntime wire variant and reconstruct all command metadata.
The shared launch facade reexports runtime allowlist and Windows candidate
behavior. Shared Windows candidates read the configured terminal, detection and
cmd fallback, not the separate app-core-only legacy override; app-core keeps
its old override behavior for its existing API.

Update guidance:
Preserve actual socket precedence, effective default paths, argument boundaries,
new-pane identity, default launch behavior, fresh-spawn and hook contracts.
Never serialize secrets, arbitrary metadata or parent terminal identity into
runtime command arguments. Keep contextual companion requests distinguishable
to older peers and preserve local fallback on their rejection. Keep SSH
handling separate. The executed-child hook regression and portable Windows logic
tests are deterministic evidence, not live cross-platform certification.

